{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/_concurrency\/asyncsequence\/deliver(to:batchbufferlimit:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deliver","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"destinations","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","text":"Destination","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"..., ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchBufferLimit","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidBatchBufferLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations23InvalidBatchBufferLimitV","text":"InvalidBatchBufferLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations8DeliveryV","text":"Delivery","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where each batch goes."}]}],"name":"destinations"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How many batches each destination may have waiting while it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still receiving an earlier one. A tenth of how many dropped batches it keeps track of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to read back."}]}],"name":"batchBufferLimit"}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The delivery, holding the unit of work that completes once the last batch is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered, and throws what the sequence throws, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when cancelled;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery\/bufferDropReports"},{"text":" report the batches full buffers drop.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination(), vendor)","try await delivery.execute()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a slow destination delays only itself. When a batch arrives while a destination’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer already holds "},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" batches, the oldest waiting batch is dropped,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"logged and reported on the delivery’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery\/bufferDropReports"},{"type":"text","text":", where the drops no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one has read yet wait as one "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" per destination. Its records kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"memory only are lost. Those a store keeps are not: once that destination has received"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every batch waiting in its buffer, the delivery reads them back from the store and hands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them to that destination alone, one dropped batch at a time, oldest first. Read back, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record is as it was dropped: its "},{"code":"EventRecord.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values and context, which the delivery keeps meanwhile. The delivery keeps track of at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most ten times "},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dropped batches per destination; past that it forgets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the oldest, whose records stay in the store for the next launch, and logs it. Once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence ends, the work completes after every destination has received its last batch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ones read back included."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store keeps (those with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord.deliveryTag"},{"type":"text","text":") are reported to it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before a batch goes to any destination, and again once every destination’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has returned for it without being cancelled, when the store may forget them. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store couldn’t mark as being delivered is left out of the batch, and a batch left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no records isn’t sent. A record that some destination never received, because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store no longer kept it or couldn’t read it back when the delivery asked, is never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"acknowledged, so a store that still keeps it delivers it on the next launch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records the delivery has read but not delivered are lost to this run when it is cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or fails. Without a store they are gone; a store never had them acknowledged, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivers them on the next launch (unless its bound drops them first, which it reports)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing runs until the work is executed, and each execution reads the sequence again, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a delivery that finished or failed can be executed again (a retry). Cancelling it drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the batches its destinations had waiting, and is permanent, as for every Afluent unit of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work: executing a cancelled delivery again throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" at once, so build a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new one instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Throws","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidBatchBufferLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when "},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is below 1."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The work of delivering each batch of this sequence to every destination, until the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence ends."}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Destinations","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"extendedModule":"_Concurrency","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Deliver.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Deliver.swift#L59"},"title":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","externalID":"s:Sci12Destinationss8SendableRzSay6Events11EventRecordVG7ElementRtzrlE7deliver2to16batchBufferLimitAA8DeliveryVAA11Destination_pd_SitAA012InvalidBatchjK0VYKF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"[EventRecord]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deliver","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP"},{"text":"..., ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchBufferLimit","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"InvalidBatchBufferLimit","kind":"typeIdenti